@startuml possession-flow-foul
' ⚠ A DETAIL DIAGRAM. The whole possession, and the second-chance LOOP that
' wraps this one, are in possession-flow.puml — read that first.
' ⚠ THIS FILE OWNS: the foul gate, the THREE labels one foul can take, the
' free-throw trip, and the live board on a missed last FT.
' ⚠ BRANCH ORDER HERE IS LOAD-BEARING: flagrant is rolled FIRST, non-shooting
' SECOND, and SHOOTING_FOUL is the FALL-THROUGH. Reordering changes the model.
' ⚠ Notes say what the flow DOES; the argument lives in possession-flow-model.md.
' Render: plantuml -DPLANTUML_LIMIT_SIZE=16384 -tpng   (every diagram is now under
'   the 4096px default, so the flag is insurance — but keep using it, and ⚠ keep each
'   diagram SCREEN-SIZED: past ~2,000px it stops being readable long before it stops
'   rendering. ⚠ `-checkonly` does not lay out and does not catch deprecated syntax
'   that renders as a warning box — look at the PNG.)
title FoulResolver — ONE foul, THREE labels\n//§3.12 all shot types · §3.14b flagrants · §3.16 composition · §3.21 the live FT board//

skinparam ActivityDiamondFontSize 11
skinparam ActivityFontSize 12
skinparam NoteFontSize 10

start
note right
   **Every** shot type can be fouled, graduated by a per-shot-type
  multiplier: DRIVE 1.0 (the anchor) ≈ POST > PERIMETER > THREE.
  ⚠ ``BASE_NO_BASKET_FOUL`` does not mean "the foul rate" — it
  means the foul STOPPED the shot, which is why trimming it moves
  points the WRONG way. A multiplier of 0.0 — not a zero base —
  is the only true off-switch.
end note

if (**foul?**\n//foulDrawing vs (20 − foulProne)//\n//× foulMultiplier(shotType)//\n//× fatigueFactor per player//) then (yes)
  :**defender.recordFoul()** — the foul is CHARGED here
  //NO event is emitted yet — the two rolls below decide WHICH//
  //foul event this becomes. Exactly ONE is ever emitted, and//
  //the charge is what holds the foul TOTAL by construction//;
  note right
    The **pre-shot** foul — the shot is stopped, a 2-FT trip
    (**3 on a THREE**), mutually exclusive with a made basket.
    The **and-1** (foul WITH a made shot) is a separate post-make
    roll — see possession-flow-shot.puml.
     **The stopped shot charges NO FGA** — this branch returns
    before recordFieldGoalAttempt().
    ⚠ **READ THE THREE-WAY SHAPE BELOW CAREFULLY — it is ONE foul with THREE possible labels, not three fouls.** ``recordFoul()``
    has ALREADY run above, so neither roll below moves the foul
    RATE; they only decide the outcome STRING and the free throws.
     **SHOOTING_FOUL is the FALL-THROUGH** — the label a foul gets
    when both rolls miss, which is why it appears LAST even though
    it is the most common. A flagrant REPLACES it; a non-shooting
    foul REPLACES it. They never compose.
  end note

  if (**FLAGRANT?**\n//P = FLAGRANT_FOULS_PER_TEAM_GAME ÷ personal fouls//\n//layered ON TOP of the foul — no rate re-partitioned//) then (yes)
    :FOUL — FLAGRANT_FOUL_1 or _2
    //15% severity sub-roll — flat, no causal input//
    charge committer //recordFoul()// — a PERSONAL foul
    on _2: //recordFlagrantTwo()// → EJECTED;
    :FREE_THROW ×**2** — *_FLAGRANT
    the FOULED player shoots
    **REPLACES the 2/3 FTs below — does NOT add**;
    :→ **OFFENSE RETAINS** → second chance
    //back to the loop in possession-flow.puml//;
    note right
       **THE POSSESSION-RETENTION FORK** — the first FT path in this
      engine that does NOT end the possession. This site is
       **always defensive**, so it always retains, under the same
      cap as every other retention path.
      ⚠ **This is a RETURN TO THE LOOP, not the end of the possession** — activity-diagram syntax cannot draw an edge
      back into the enclosing ``repeat`` from inside a partition.
    end note
    stop
  endif

  if (**NON-SHOOTING FOUL?**\n//flat sim.non-shooting-foul-share, NO skill input//\n//a SECOND roll on the foul already charged above//) then (yes)
    :FOUL — **NON_SHOOTING_FOUL**
    //the foul was ALREADY charged above — this only re-labels it//
    counts toward the bonus AND FOUL_OUT_LIMIT;
    note right
       **Layered, not carved** — the ``isFoul`` roll above is
      UNCHANGED and ``recordFoul()`` has already run, so **the foul TOTAL holds by construction.**
      ⚠ **Order matters: flagrant is rolled FIRST**, so a flagrant
      common foul is simply a flagrant — the two never compose.
      ⚠ **THE POSSESSION ENDS AND THE BALL DOES NOT COME BACK, AND THAT IS DELIBERATELY WRONG AS BASKETBALL.** A real common foul
      is a side inbound: the offense keeps the ball. Every returning
      variant would yield a live attempt where the stopped shot
      charged none, and FGA has no headroom for it.
    end note
    if (committing team already in the penalty?\n//GameData.isInBonus — emit-then-count//) then (yes)
      :FREE_THROW ×**2** — BONUS
      //the fouled team shoots//;
    else (no)
      :**no free throws** — the point of the phase;
    endif
    :**possession over**;
    stop
  endif

  :FOUL — **SHOOTING_FOUL**
  //THE FALL-THROUGH: both rolls above missed//
  primaryPlayerId = the DEFENDER who committed it
  **opponentPlayerId = the FOULED SHOOTER**;
  note right
    ⚠ **The counterparty's ORIENTATION FLIPS here** relative to the
    steal and the block. There, primary is the victim and the
    opponent is the defender who acted; here primary is the
    COMMITTER, so the opponent is on OFFENSE. The rule that
    survives every site: **opponent is ALWAYS the opposite team from primary.** A teammate never goes here.
    ⚠ On EVERY FOUL event primaryPlayerId is the COMMITTER — the
    inverse of SHOT/TURNOVER, where primary is the victim.
    Test-enforced.
  end note

  repeat
    if (free throw made?\n//freeThrows skill//) then (yes)
      :FREE_THROW — MADE_SHOOTING
      +1 point;
    else (no)
      :FREE_THROW — MISSED_SHOOTING;
    endif
  repeat while (**more attempts in the trip?**\n//3 for a fouled THREE, else 2//) is (yes) not (no)
  note right
    ⚠ **The COUNT is a RULE on ShotType, not a tunable.**
    A stopped THREE = **3** FTs.
    ⚠ **If this foul had turned FLAGRANT the count is a flat 2** —
    so a flagrant stopped THREE awards FEWER FTs than the ordinary
    foul it upgraded. Correct by rule, counter-intuitive, and
     **NOT to be "fixed" into 3 + 2.**
  end note

  if (**last FT of the trip, AND missed?**\n//the last attempt is LIVE by rule//) then (yes)
    :resolve the board through **MissedShotResolver**
    //reused WHOLE — see possession-flow-rebound.puml//;
    note right
      ⚠ **ONLY THE LAST ATTEMPT IS LIVE.** A missed FIRST FT is a
      dead ball; non-last misses are LARGER in number than live
      ones, so the terminal test is the whole correctness here.
      ⚠ **TWO SOURCES ARE EXCLUDED BY RULE** — FLAGRANT (the offense
      already RETAINS) and TECHNICAL (play resumes with the ball as
      it was). **They are absent from this fork rather than drawn as a "no" leg**, because their possession consequence is fixed by
      rule, independent of the FT outcome.
      ⚠ **The contest is the ORDINARY board contest at a REDUCED base** (``× FREE_THROW_REBOUND_LEAN``): the defense has inside
      position **by rule**, so the realized offensive share is
      ~**0.19**, not the board's 0.262. That lean is a
      ``public static final`` **RULE constant, NOT a tunable.**
      ⚠ **An OFFENSIVE board here RETURNS THE BALL** → the same
      retention the offensive rebound uses, under the SAME cap.
    end note
    :→ offense may **RETAIN**
    //back to the loop in possession-flow.puml//;
    stop
  else (no — dead ball, or an excluded source)
    :**possession over**;
    stop
  endif

else (no)
  :→ on to ShotResolver
  //possession-flow.puml//;
  stop
endif
@enduml
